# The list that completes what is typed (scenes/parts.seed.ts writes the note into a scratch outline): a block
# opened to be written and a property's name begun. One box hung under the token's start: each row a tag for what
# it is, its name with the typed letters set apart, and one quiet detail; in its foot, which row of how many is lit
# and what the keys do. Beside it, the card: what the lit row says of itself.
bar.open scope=search query="Frost fleece"
bar.pick n=1
edit
draft.paste text=" [hea"
complete.move by=1
